      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason is that for ISH enabled builds, we would like sensors inactive during system suspend. This ensures that SoC can enter into S0I2.2. We changed active-mask \u003d \"SENSOR_ACTIVE_S0_S3\" to active-mask \u003d \"SENSOR_ACTIVE_S0\".\n\nIn case of sensors on EC, SoC is not impacted even if sensors are active during system suspend.",
